+
+## Table geometry and UI persistence
+
+A card's `corner-v2` layout anchor is its upright bottom-left corner. A -90-degree rotation leaves that point at the tapped bottom-right corner. Old top-left layout coordinates are migrated for display. Zone moves and casts carry a pending placement through the core action; the UI does not force-move a card to make a drag look successful.
+
+Canonical card picking ignores hover paint elevation. Drop ordering uses pointer intersection and overlap to support inserting a card between existing layers. Normalized grab points preserve exact placement across zoom and tapping. Tests verify the actual browser rectangles during the drag and after release, as well as visual undo/redo.
+
+Panel geometry and camera state live in validated `uiLayout`, not in the rules state. The exported session also contains `tableView` for stable implicit card placement. Browser preferences are independent of new game construction; imported sessions retain their own game settings. Saved preference comparisons use values, not JSON object-key ordering. Explicit popup positions are respected; automatic positions avoid other popups and respond to size changes, including local image decoding and expanding rules text.
+
+The 1.1 interface retains rules-pack/session compatibility with 1.0. Future incompatible rules-state changes must still bump the rules-pack identifier. New games default to no held priority and explicit reserve access enabled; imported games keep their settings. The ordinary core API remains independent of those interface defaults.
 
